            <value>At 7:05 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Saturday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for Western Quebec. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Pontiac. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
